            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "angelface"
            },
            "reviewBody": "To make it gluten free I used 1/2 cup tapioca flour. I used honey instead of sugar at the ratio 2/3 cup honey for each cup of sugar and reduced the liquid by 1/4 cup for every cup of honey used.. I was quite pleased with the results.",
            "datePublished": "2016-06-19T02:33:56.147Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Moth612"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I turned this basic recipe into a pie by simply decreasing the milk a little bit and adding a couple extra egg yolks. Then I just put it in a double crust and followed the baking directions. There's a bit of extra filling, but I just put that in a plain pan and it tastes great as a little extra treat. I've tried a number of rhubarb custard pie recipes, but this is my favorite!",
